# --- Runtime trees: code only, never the data it operates on ----------------
# Matched BY NAME at any depth, not by the one path they use today. Both
# locations are configurable — FTI_TRAINING_RUNTIME_DIR and FTI_DATA_DIR — and
# feature_pipeline_hub/.gitignore only covers the defaults, so pointing either
# somewhere else inside the repo would silently drop 68 GB of weights, runs and
# source photographs out from under the rules.
#
# training_runtime/ is the model copy (~40 GB), the dedicated venv, the latent
# cache and every run's checkpoints. It is rebuilt by
# scripts/setup_training_runtime.sh — that script is the code, this tree is not.
training_runtime/

# Ingested and derived images. Contents only, so the deeper .gitignore can still
# re-include its .gitkeep skeleton (a rule in a nested .gitignore overrides this
# one, but only if the directory itself was never excluded).
**/data/raw/**
**/data/processed/**

# --- Datasets & media -------------------------------------------------------
# This is an ML dataset-curation project: images and captions are data, never
# source. Dataset folders keep only their .gitkeep skeleton (see
# feature_pipeline_hub/.gitignore); everything else below is ignored outright.
datasets/
dataset/
exports/
snapshots/
fti_upload_*/

# Media files anywhere in the tree. If you ever need to commit a real asset
# (a logo, a doc screenshot), add it explicitly with: git add -f <path>
#
# Written as character classes because gitignore matching is CASE-SENSITIVE on
# Linux and macOS-with-a-case-sensitive-volume: a plain `*.jpg` does not match
# `IMG_4021.JPG`, which is exactly what every phone and camera produces. There
# are 39 such files in data/raw today, saved only by the directory rules in
# feature_pipeline_hub/.gitignore — this is the second line of defence, so it
# has to hold on its own. `.suffix.lower()` in storage.py/validators.py is why
# the app happily ingests them in the first place.
*.[pP][nN][gG]
*.[jJ][pP][gG]
*.[jJ][pP][eE][gG]
*.[jJ][fF][iI][fF]
*.[wW][eE][bB][pP]
*.[gG][iI][fF]
*.[bB][mM][pP]
*.[tT][iI][fF]
*.[tT][iI][fF][fF]
*.[hH][eE][iI][cC]
*.[hH][eE][iI][fF]
*.[aA][vV][iI][fF]
*.[pP][sS][dD]
# Not *.svg: no camera or dataset produces one, and docs/training-architecture.svg
# is a tracked diagram — ignoring the extension would only get in the way.
# Camera raw: not ingestible by the app, but an operator's source folder is full
# of them and they carry the same faces plus GPS in EXIF.
*.[dD][nN][gG]
*.[cC][rR]2
*.[nN][eE][fF]
*.[aA][rR][wW]
*.[oO][rR][fF]
*.[rR][wW]2
*.[mM][pP]4
*.[mM][oO][vV]
*.[aA][vV][iI]
*.[wW][eE][bB][mM]
*.[mM][kK][vV]

# Caption sidecars that ship next to training images.
#
# `.txt` is the format the exporter actually writes (`.caption` is the other
# convention, kept for imported datasets). Ignoring it wholesale is deliberate:
# a caption in this project is a detailed physical description of a real person,
# so it is more identifying than the filename and about as identifying as the
# image. Nothing in this repo tracks a .txt today; if that ever changes, the
# `git add -f` escape hatch above applies here too.
*.caption
*.txt

# Curation artefacts: not images, but they list every filename in a dataset.
curation_report.json
curation_overrides.json

# --- Model & artifact formats ----------------------------------------------
*.safetensors
*.ckpt
*.pt
*.pth
*.bin
*.onnx
*.parquet
*.arrow
*.npy
*.npz

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Databases & local state ------------------------------------------------
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# --- Secrets ----------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets.toml

# --- Tooling & editors ------------------------------------------------------
.claude/
.streamlit/secrets.toml
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# --- OS junk ----------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# AppleDouble sidecars: macOS writes these next to real files when copying to
# non-HFS volumes, so they show up shadowing source files (e.g. ._gallery.py).
._*
